    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jet.2026.106207",
      "sequence": 3,
      "source_sequence": 3,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Reference-dependent choice bracketing",
      "title_cn": "参照依赖的选择分组",
      "authors": [
        "Pauline Vorjohann"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "I derive a model of choice bracketing from two behavioral axioms in an expected utility framework. The first behavioral axiom establishes a link between narrow bracketing and correlation neglect. The second behavioral axiom identifies the reference point as the connector between broad and narrow preferences. The narrow bracketer is characterized by an inability to process changes from the reference point in different dimensions simultaneously. As a result, her tradeoffs between dimensions are distorted. She evaluates dimensions in isolation, implying a disregard for how they affect one another. When evaluating a dimension, she remains anchored to the reference point in the respective other dimension. This implies that she mistakenly perceives preference interactions in relation to the reference point. I present applications to portfolio choice, consumption bundle choice, and an exchange economy.",
      "abstract_cn": "我在期望效用框架下，从二行为公理推导出选择分组模型。第一行为公理建立了狭义分组与相关性忽视之间的联系。第二行为公理将参照点确定为广义偏好与狭义偏好之间的连接点。狭义分组者的特征是无法同时处理来自参照点在不同维度上的变化。因此，她在维度之间的权衡被扭曲。她孤立地评估各维度，意味着忽视了它们如何相互影响一。在评估某一维度时，她仍锚定于相应其他维度的参照点。这意味着她错误地将偏好交互视为与参照点相关。我展示了该模型在投资组合选择、消费组合选择及交换经济中的应用。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jet.2026.106207",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022053126000700?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
