    {
      "paper_id": "doi:10.1016/j.jet.2026.106203",
      "sequence": 7,
      "source_sequence": 7,
      "article_type": "research-article",
      "title_en": "Learning through imitation: An experiment",
      "title_cn": "通过模仿学习：一项实验",
      "authors": [
        "Marina Agranov",
        "Gabriel Lopez-Moctezuma",
        "Philipp Strack",
        "Omer Tamuz"
      ],
      "abstract_en": "We compare how well agents aggregate information in two repeated social learning environments. In the first setting agents have access to a public data set. In the second they have access to the same data, and also to the past actions of others. Despite the fact that actions contain no additional payoff-relevant information, and despite potential herd behavior, free riding and information overload issues, observing and imitating the actions of others leads agents to take the optimal action more often in the second setting. We also investigate the effect of group size, as well as a setting in which agents observe private data and others’ actions.",
      "abstract_cn": "我们比较了代理人在二重复社会学习环境中聚合信息的效果。在第一环境中，代理人可以访问一个公共数据集。在第二环境中，他们不仅可以访问相同的数据，还可以观察他人的过去行为。尽管这些行为不包含额外的与收益相关的信息，且存在潜在的羊群效应、搭便车和信息过载问题，观察并模仿他人的行为仍使代理人在第二环境中更频繁地采取最优行动。我们还研究了群体规模的影响，以及代理人观察私人数据和他人行为的情形。",
      "abstract_snippet_en": "",
      "doi": "10.1016/j.jet.2026.106203",
      "source_url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022053126000669?dgcid=rss_sd_all",
